{
  "id": "COMPOUND:27259 - PROTEIN:5005",
  "verbalization": "Sophoraflavanone A is implicated in the biological activity of HCT-8 cells through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Sophoraflavanone A acts as a target for ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Cytisine, N-formyl- and Galbanic Acid. These targets are all involved in cellular processes that ultimately lead to interactions with HCT-8 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Sophoraflavanone A may influence HCT-8 cell behavior, possibly through the modulation of transporters or other cellular functions. The shared involvement of ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 across different targets underscores a recurring mechanism in the biological response to these compounds, suggesting a possible role in drug action or cellular signaling.",
